{"kind":"assert","text":"New fact on my serve.md scope question at 24511b89, which I think answers it, and I am still not acting on it until you say so.\n\nI had assumed the false sentence was pre-existing prose this lane happened to sit next to. It is not. `git diff origin/main HEAD -- docs/reference/gs/serve.md` at the recut head shows it inside the lane's own added block:\n\n  +The remote is read from the repository's own configuration only —\n  +`git config --local` — so configuration outside the repository cannot say\n  +where the repository lives.\n\nThis lane wrote that sentence. It is not documentation the repair happens to contradict; it is the lane publishing its own reasoning about its own security property, and the repair in the same lane proves the reasoning wrong. So correcting it is not reaching into a page the row does not cover — it is the lane finishing a sentence it started.\n\nThat is why I think the answer is yes, and it is also why I am not treating my own argument as the authorization. The distinction between \"this is clearly implied\" and \"this is granted\" is the one that cost this lane three rounds, and a persuasive reading of my own is exactly what it looked like each time.\n\nONE MORE SENTENCE IN THE SAME BLOCK, which the repair has already made true and which I mention so the record is complete: \"A URL carrying userinfo, a query or a fragment is declined outright rather than stripped.\" That was false at 7da8b753 for a bare trailing \"#\", which Go silently normalised away rather than declining. The raw-delimiter fix makes it true as written, so it needs no edit — it just needed the code to catch up with it.\n\nWHERE THE HEAD STANDS. Recut onto current main c679fb73 at 65d46115, tree 42edf43f, worktree clean, three commits each carrying its own Rests-On. I verified by hand that the merge's work survived — Publish.tsx, authority.ts, modalFocus.ts, records.ts and the six new ui tests are present, and publishRefusal, decideSupersede, signingRefusal, buildRecordIndex and satisfier all still resolve — and that the lane survived, with eight repositoryLocalGit references and webRemoteURL still testing the raw string. My own gate run at this head is in flight; I will report those numbers rather than the ones from the pre-recut base.\n\nNothing is published and no review is requested. If you say yes, the sentence changes and the head moves once more before either happens."}